# === Effy monorepo .gitignore ===

# --- OS / editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# --- Secrets / env (never commit) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Kotlin / Gradle / Android (apps/customer-mobile) ---
.gradle/
**/build/
local.properties
*.hprof
captures/
.kotlin/

# --- iOS / Xcode (apps/customer-mobile/iosApp) ---
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/
.swiftpm/
Pods/

# --- Go (services/api) ---
*.exe
*.test
*.out
vendor/
/services/api/bin/

# --- Node / TS (infra lambdas + reserved web) ---
node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.pnpm-store/

# ⚠ EXCEPTION (038): packages/email-kit/dist/ is a COMMITTED, DRIFT-GUARDED artifact, not a build
# output. `make email-check` regenerates it and fails if the contents changed — which is only
# meaningful if the previous contents are in the repository. Same rule as design-system's committed
# Compose theme and @effy/brand's 57 committed assets; those escape this pattern only because they
# do not live in a directory called `dist`.
# ⚠ dist/preview/ IS a build output and stays ignored — it is regenerated on demand and would
# otherwise put seven rendered HTML pages into every diff.
# ⚠ BOTH lines are required. Git will not descend into an excluded directory, so re-including the
# directory alone is not enough — the `/**` line is what actually re-includes the files. Verified
# with `git check-ignore -v`, because the one-line version looks correct and silently does nothing.
!packages/email-kit/dist/
!packages/email-kit/dist/**
packages/email-kit/dist/preview/

# --- Terraform (infra) ---
# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl and *.tfvars are COMMITTED on purpose — reproducible provider
# versions and per-env config are code; no secrets live in tfvars (spec 001-infra-foundation).
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
*.tfplan
.turbo

# --- Firebase client config (050-observability-push-foundation) ---
# Per-app, per-env build inputs supplied by the operator — NOT committed (FR-031).
# A missing file makes the mobile build fail loudly rather than ship a wrong default.
**/androidApp/google-services.json
**/iosApp/GoogleService-Info.plist

# --- Serverless Framework build output (054-product-inventory) ---
# ⚠ AT THE ROOT DELIBERATELY, not per-service. Protection used to depend on each edge service
# carrying its own .gitignore, and that discipline has failed twice: `edge-api/notifications` never
# had one and committed 2.9 MB of build output — including a `serverless-state.json` carrying the
# resolved RDS hostname, master username and secret ARN — and `edge-api/orders` (053) has none
# either and is still untracked, so it would have leaked the same on its first commit.
# A rule here covers every service that exists and every one that will.
**/.serverless/
**/.esbuild/
